WEBVTT

1
00:00:03.383 --> 00:00:07.943
Does piriform cortex just scatter its input, or does it add something of its own?

2
00:00:08.933 --> 00:00:13.913
Pashkovski and colleagues imaged two things in mice, with the same panel of odours

3
00:00:13.913 --> 00:00:14.913
for the comparison.

4
00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:19.247
First, bulb axon boutons inside piriform cortex.

5
00:00:20.247 --> 00:00:24.227
These are the terminals of mitral and tufted cells, the cortex's input.

6
00:00:25.217 --> 00:00:29.577
Second, piriform neurons in layer 2/3, the cortex's output.

7
00:00:30.600 --> 00:00:32.940
The mice breathed at a controlled sniff rate.

8
00:00:33.883 --> 00:00:35.083
Pause and predict.

9
00:00:36.023 --> 00:00:40.623
If piriform followed our simple random model, how should related odours compare

10
00:00:40.623 --> 00:00:42.123
between boutons and cortex?

11
00:00:48.317 --> 00:00:52.177
By that model, the cortex should largely keep the bulb's relationships.

12
00:00:53.377 --> 00:00:56.457
Related odours should be less alike than in the input, not more.

13
00:00:57.417 --> 00:00:58.697
The first half held.

14
00:00:59.537 --> 00:01:04.577
In boutons and in cortex, related odours gave more similar patterns than unrelated

15
00:01:04.577 --> 00:01:05.577
ones.

16
00:01:06.067 --> 00:01:08.187
The scattered cortex kept the chemistry.

17
00:01:09.217 --> 00:01:10.957
The second half did not hold.

18
00:01:11.917 --> 00:01:16.497
Piriform neurons clustered related odours more tightly than their own input did.

19
00:01:17.450 --> 00:01:19.870
Made-up numbers on screen show the direction.

20
00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.370
The cortex value sits above the input value.

21
00:01:24.333 --> 00:01:28.393
The authors also fed their bouton data through a random-wiring model.

22
00:01:29.193 --> 00:01:31.673
It kept the order, but made the patterns less alike.

23
00:01:32.717 --> 00:01:37.257
So something in the cortex added structure that the random model did not give.

24
00:01:38.250 --> 00:01:39.950
This is a different kind of map.

25
00:01:40.810 --> 00:01:43.730
A spatial map puts similar odours in nearby places.

26
00:01:44.833 --> 00:01:49.793
A representational geometry gives similar odours similar population patterns,

27
00:01:50.233 --> 00:01:51.233
wherever the cells sit.

28
00:01:52.183 --> 00:01:55.163
Piriform cortex has the second without the first.

29
00:01:56.183 --> 00:01:57.463
What could add the structure?

30
00:01:58.463 --> 00:02:03.543
Piriform pyramidal cells, its main excitatory neurons, are linked to each other by

31
00:02:03.543 --> 00:02:04.583
association fibres.

32
00:02:05.717 --> 00:02:08.557
These are recurrent connections within the cortex.

33
00:02:09.817 --> 00:02:12.237
Reviews treat them as a place where experience is stored.

34
00:02:13.250 --> 00:02:18.010
Strengthening synapses among neurons that are active together is thought to bind a

35
00:02:18.010 --> 00:02:20.390
scattered ensemble into a familiar odour.

36
00:02:21.433 --> 00:02:25.693
Then the whole ensemble could respond even when part of the input is missing.

37
00:02:26.553 --> 00:02:27.733
This is pattern completion.

38
00:02:28.833 --> 00:02:31.613
Pashkovski's team tested the network directly.

39
00:02:32.493 --> 00:02:36.793
A genetic tool blocked transmitter release from excitatory piriform neurons.

40
00:02:37.867 --> 00:02:41.047
Their bulb input still arrived, so they still responded.

41
00:02:41.927 --> 00:02:45.707
But they excited their neighbours, including inhibitory cells, much less.

42
00:02:46.750 --> 00:02:47.950
Pause and predict.

43
00:02:47.950 --> 00:02:52.850
With the network weakened, what should happen to the cortex's odour relationships?

44
00:02:58.983 --> 00:03:01.743
Its odour relationships became more like the bulb's.

45
00:03:02.783 --> 00:03:04.803
Responses did not simply weaken.

46
00:03:05.783 --> 00:03:10.123
Tuning broadened and correlations rose overall, yet the pattern moved toward the

47
00:03:10.123 --> 00:03:11.123
bulb's.

48
00:03:11.433 --> 00:03:17.073
One caveat. Piriform also sends feedback to the bulb, and connects to other

49
00:03:17.073 --> 00:03:18.093
olfactory areas.

50
00:03:19.133 --> 00:03:22.533
So piriform network activity is needed for the change.

51
00:03:23.433 --> 00:03:26.413
It is not shown that local connections alone produce it.

52
00:03:27.333 --> 00:03:31.593
The cortex keeps the bulb's chemistry, then reshapes it with its own network.
